# Goal 9: Fix lgamma / lgammaf — signgam not set

## Functions
`lgamma` (double), `lgammaf` (float)

## Source files
- C (double): /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathd/lgammad.c
- C (float): /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathf/lgammaf.c (and internal/gammaf.c for __lgammaf)
- Rust: /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s3/src/mathd.rs (lgamma), /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s3/src/mathf.rs (lgammaf)

## Problem
lgamma and lgammaf always return signgam=0 instead of the correct sign:
- lgamma(1) → signgam should be 1, got 0
- lgamma(2) → signgam should be 1, got 0
- lgamma(0.5) → signgam should be 1, got 0
- lgamma(-0.5) → signgam should be -1, got 0
- lgammaf shows same pattern (all signgam=0)

The computed lgamma values are correct; only signgam is wrong.

## What needs to change
The Rust implementation likely doesn't write to the global `signgam` variable. In C, lgamma sets a global `extern int signgam`. The Rust bridge must write this value through the FFI. Check how the Rust bridge exposes signgam and ensure the lgamma/lgammaf functions actually set it.

## Success Criteria
- All lgamma tests produce correct signgam values (1 or -1, matching C)
- All lgammaf tests produce correct signgam values
- lgamma/lgammaf computed values remain correct
